The BF16 LFM3 presets for CUDA, ROCm, and Furiosa RNGD use upstream source test
reports. The Metal preset uses batch size 1 as in ZML's M3 Max benchmark.
Hardware validation of the generated Docker commands for these source-tested
presets is pending.

The [20261106.0 release notes](https://zml.ai/posts/llmd-20261106.0/)
list additional model families. Check [Docker Hub](https://hub.docker.com/r/zmlai/llmd/tags)
for backend tags or the [ZML tap](https://github.com/zml/homebrew-zml)
for the current Metal package.

# [Next steps]($heading.id('next-steps'))

Choose **Configure launch** for a recipe to preselect its checkpoint and
backend in the [LLMD quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart')). There you can
choose a model source and generate the commands.
